    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only executable test class, and both tests pass with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field (`'<TIER>_<AREA>'`) with minimal structural impact:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` property to the Owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`Segments.java`** (new, small cohesive util) \u2014 a single static `of(int membershipLevel, String locality)` that returns `PREMIUM`/`STANDARD` (level \u2265 3) joined with `METRO`/`REGIONAL` (locality in {NSW, VIC, QLD}). WMC_other is 0 and CC is low.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to `Segments.of(...)`, reusing the existing `Membership.level`/`Membership.points` and `CustomerCodes.regionOf` derivations that already back the `membershipLevel` and `locality` DTO fields \u2014 so the segment stays consistent with those and no existing method grew.\n\nThe tier/area logic lives in its own tiny class rather than being grown inside an existing method, keeping every touched function simple.",
